# Credentials and per-user configuration. Never commit.
.Renviron

# Quarto build output. _freeze/ is deliberately NOT here: it is committed, so
# CI can render the whole site with no R installed and no credentials, and
# therefore cannot reach Databricks. Editing an example page invalidates its
# freeze hash, so re-render locally and commit the result with the edit.
/_site/

# Rendered output that lands at the repo root rather than in _site/. Quarto
# writes here when it is invoked on a single file from the project root, and
# /_site/ above does not cover it. Committing these once was enough: they are
# build artefacts, they rot against the source, and CI rebuilds the site from
# scratch anyway.
/site_libs/
/index.html
/*/*.html
/*/*_files/
/.quarto/

# R
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
renv/library/
renv/local/
renv/cellar/
renv/lock/
renv/python/
renv/sandbox/
renv/staging/

# Working design documents. Local only: they carry personal annotation and
# references to the engagement that produced the findings, neither of which
# belongs in a public repo. See docs/README.md.
/docs/

**/*.quarto_ipynb

# knitr's intermediate, left behind in example/ when a render is interrupted.
# It is a near-copy of the .qmd beside it, so it rots against the source and
# reads as a second, stale version of a page.
**/*.rmarkdown

# Compute targets. config.yml carries a real warehouse and cluster id, and this
# repo is public by default, so it stays local. dbx-config.R reads it and is
# safe to track; the ids never appear in the helper itself.
config.yml

# Stage-to-stage artefacts of the worked example are committed, not ignored.
# Each stage saves what the next one reads, and `bootstrap.qmd` reads three of
# them in its setup chunk, above its `eval` gate, so without them a copy edit
# cannot be re-rendered without a cluster. 9.4M in plain git, not LFS: they
# change rarely, which is the case LFS does not serve.

# The one exception: results.qmd writes this to demonstrate saving a result
# table, and no page reads it back, so it is a byproduct of the render rather
# than a stage-to-stage artefact.
flow_variability_results.rds

# Python bytecode from scripts/ and .claude/skills/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# knitr intermediate, left behind by an interrupted render
*.knit.md
